        "note": "JSONL dispatch coordinates replay, negotiation and oracle operations. Selected replay/admission paths use the pure protocol step; async jobs use their own checked transitions."
      },
      {
        "id": "compiler",
        "label": "Model-interface compilation",
        "focus": [
          "inputs",
          "frontend",
          "resolver",
          "generated",
          "clients"
        ],
        "note": "Captured sources, reviewed contract and ITF evidence produce semantic locks, typed bindings and corpora. Eight emitters cover TS sync/async v1/v2, C++ v1/v2, Rust v1/v2 and Lean v1. Node suite/project bundle publication stays async v1. Read-only lock comparison reports migration requirements."
      },
      {
        "id": "application",
        "label": "Application ownership",
        "focus": [
          "generated",
          "clients",
          "application",
          "gate",
          "transports",
          "session"
        ],
        "note": "SDKs own admitted replay and binding lifetime. Applications supply actual operations/state and safe hooks. Optional cooperative DPM controls C++/Rust threads and Node workers; Gate independently owns Linux/Bubblewrap Node/Rust isolation. Generic DPM Gate integration is not implied."
      },
      {
        "id": "verified-core",
        "label": "Pure laws and proof boundary",
        "focus": [
          "frontend",
          "resolver",
          "core",
          "codec"
        ],
        "note": "Selected pure transitions, equality/diff/trace laws, policy and codecs have machine-checked properties. Protocol refinement is to a Lean-encoded tag relation; it does not prove arbitrary Shell, OS or Apalache execution."
      },
      {
        "id": "effect-boundary",
        "label": "Runtime effects and shared resources",
        "focus": [
          "cli",
          "transports",
          "session",
          "interfaces",
          "jobs",
          "adapter",
          "capture",
          "ffi",
          "registry",
          "consul",
          "apalache"
        ],
        "note": "Connection workers share a job store and interface service. Connection capacity, live-job permits and descriptor-resolution limits are distinct. Capture and delivery preserve bounded wire results and explicit path scope."
      },
      {
        "id": "qualification",
        "label": "Distribution and evidence",
        "focus": [
          "catalog",
          "distribution",
          "qualification",
          "evidence",
          "clients"
        ],
        "note": "Frozen source/dependency identities feed snapshots, verified caches and transactional installs. The October 7 named profile passed 18 commands/16 tiers, two D bindings, 19 scope nodes, 20 bundles and six controls. Unknown publication/hosted-CI and broader M4 claims remain separate."
      },
      {
        "id": "dpm",
        "label": "Deterministic checkpoint scheduling",
        "focus": [
          "generated",
          "clients",
          "application",
          "session",
          "core"
        ],
        "note": "A handwritten generated port maps a model action to an admitted binding-session interval. The coordinator permits one participating actor, verifies actual checkpoint arrival and observes real quiescent SUT state. Application hooks are intrusive; arbitrary preemption and external effects stay outside the profile."
      }
    ],
